      "text": "We start with the given equation:\n\\[ x - \\frac{1}{x} = 4 \\]\n\nTo find \\( x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\), we will use the identity for the cube of a binomial and other algebraic manipulations. First, let's find \\( x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} \\).\n\nStarting from \\( x - \\frac{1}{x} = 4 \\), we square both sides to get:\n\\[ \\left( x - \\frac{1}{x} \\right)^2 = 4^2 \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 2 \\cdot x \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 16 \\]\n\\[ x^2 - 2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 16 \\]\n\\[ x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 16 + 2 \\]\n\\[ x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} = 18 \\]\n\nNext, we use the identity for the cube of a sum:\n\\[ \\left( x - \\frac{1}{x} \\right)^3 = x^3 - 3x \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\left( x - \\frac{1}{x} \\right) - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\]\n\\[ x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 3 \\left( x - \\frac{1}{x} \\right) = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 3 \\cdot 4 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 12 \\]\n\\[ x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 12 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\]\n\\[ x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 12 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\]\n\\[ x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 12 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\]\n\\[ x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 12 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\]\n\\[ x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} - 12 = x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\]\n\nNow, we solve for \\( x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\):\n\\[ x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} = 36 \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x^3 - \\frac{1}{x^3} \\) is \\(\\boxed{36}\\).",
